382.m:
Created by him, they [dwell] on Kailāsa […]
And half of twenty crores of vināyakas and rudras;
and he created Skanda to destroy the one named Nāraka.
In this manner that lord Rudra has been proclaimed to you by me.
I shall tell of the secondary creation of Marīci and the others; listen to me.
The creatures, from the gods down to immovable things, were created by Svayambhū;
when all those creatures of the wise [Brahmā] did not multiply,
then he created mind-born sons equal to himself:
Marīci, Atri, Aṅgiras, Pulastya, Pulaha, Kratu,
Pracetas, Vasiṣṭha, and […] of great intellect;
these nine are determined in the Purāṇa as Brahmās.
And Agni and the ancestors are the two mind-born sons of Brahmā.
At the time of creation, O fortunate one, [he created] Dharma and Svāyambhuva Manu;
